_{44} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186392470 :answer/value "2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392471 :answer/value "-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392472 :answer/value "2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392473 :answer/value "4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392474 :answer/value "2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392515 :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+(-3)y+1z &=1 \\\\ 4x+0y+(-1)z &=-3 \\\\ 1x+(-1)y+1z &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186392517 :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392518 :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392519 :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392520 :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392521 :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392528 :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{22}$ equal to zero.*"] [17592186392528 :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{22}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 & 4\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186392530 :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392531 :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}"] [17592186392532 :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}"]}
